overnment uh does have to come to a  decision and we did um we came to a  decision as a caucus uh and and we  blended all of that with ultimately uh  the the the public health orders uh that  we have in place uh the effectiveness of  those public health orders and the uh  you know ultimately the the advice that  we that we continue to receive uh from  all of those in the in the health sector  and so they you know the decision has  been made by uh government to move  forward in this fashion to lay out this  uh you know that what the next three  weeks look like in saskatchewan uh we  feel we're able to get to this point  because of what saskatchewan people have  done as individuals and collectively as  a  society and and we're positive uh we're  confident pardon me  we're confident that uh you know this is  a is this is a path that is is good for  saskatchewan and will be supported  ultimately by the the majority of the  people in the province  and we have time for one more operator  we have murray mandrake with leader post  good morning mr premier  uh twenty four thousand six hundred  people  uh  were added to the job role in january uh  which i think you noted  that suggests that whatever you've been  doing economically at least in relation  to  uh the uh policies related to vaccines  and passports and masking has worked or  it was working so i guess what i want to  know is from an economic standpoint  what's the justification to changing  things now if what you were doing is  actually kind of working i don't i you  know and thank you for noting the fact  that uh we have had an eye to the opera  you know expanding our our economic  opportunities uh throughout this  pandemic and when you blend that with uh  some of the data that dr shahab had  provided uh with respect to how  saskatchewan people have conducted  themselves through the last number of  months and and how that is manifested in  in uh a lower uh rate of of uh  hospitalizations that that we were  expecting in the province um you know  kudos to to the people of this province  because they have allowed in doing so  have allowed our our economy to continue  to expand and a number of jobs to become  available when you look ahead  uh  and and the investments that are you  know already committed to the province  and some of that work is already  underway uh in here in in regina and at  other sites um and and more to come i i  would say more investments uh to come in  the uh in the weeks in the months ahead  that saskatchewan has a you know a great  opportunity not only to find our way uh  through the the last public health  measures we have in this omicron wave  but to find our way uh  as a as a leader in this nation and  around the world in  the global economic recovery that  ultimately is likely already underway  saskatchewan most certainly is going to  participate in that  one of the other aspects is not directly  economically related  but very much is something that we've  heard uh from from people myself as an  mla as well as a number of other  government mlas and i suspect opposition  mlas uh as as well is uh  they just  they do want things to get back to  normal but they do want things um to uh  get back to normal in a  in in maybe a bold way but most  certainly a responsible way and that's  why we've laid out uh the next number of  weeks that's why we're not just removing  things uh here today we've laid out the  next number of weeks of  of uh where the decision  where the  where the public health orders will  actually be removed in a in a phased  fashion and and that's why today i've  spoken at great length that  we have another job to do with  saskatchewan people and that's that's  really to come together in an  unjudgmental way  to accept you know our friends and  family for the decisions that they've  made  and most certainly don't you know don't  lose a friend or a family member  due to this to this virus  we have an opportunity uh to really  be an understanding uh individual and  thereby  together an understanding society and  and really  you know in many ways i think lead our  nation through uh what is a very  divisive time right now  and last question mary  i think people have come together though  if you look at the if you look at the  number people have actually gone out and  get vaccinated what today's policy does  is placate those that don't want to get  vaccinated and i get that the  frustration and the struggle to get them  vaccinated but isn't that the source of  the problem the fights in the family uh  are over whether uh the outliers will  get vaccinated and put  other people at risk and we have a  thousand deaths so i guess the question  is what is the definition of bringing  saskatchewan people together when  saskatchewan people together come  together on the notion of getting  vaccinated doing the right thing and  today's policy seems to basically say  well if you didn't do the right thing  we're no longer uh going to do anything  that can do or we can there's no longer  anything we can do to enforce that how  is that i guess bringing people together  yeah the the just the basis of your  question actually murray i think speaks  to um  you know really the the challenge that  we need to get through in in ultimately  judging you know people in the in the  pro in in the province and in our  communities um just be whether or not  you got vaccinated is not the right  thing um  there are many people that have went out  and gotten vaccinated who disagree with  the divisions that come about from a  proof of vaccination policy or proof of  negative test policy and so what we are  doing here today is is saying that we  are going to move forward without that  policy we're going to understand that  each of us has made our our own  decisions on whether they're vaccinated  or not on whether they're going to wear  a mask or not post  february 28th and that's fine we accept  that decision and we respect you for  making that decision um and that's  that's totally fine um that is your  decision to make it's not for me uh to  make that decision for you nor is it for  me to comment on on what your uh  ultimate uh decision is um this is and  we're providing that plan on on on the  steps that we're going to take in the  next number of weeks and i'm asking  saskatchewan residents to most certainly  i think about how they are going to you  know address people if they see them  with a mask or or engage with their with  their family and friends in the days  ahead i think i would further ask  outside of the province of saskatchewan  and because we still will have mandates  here we still will have our federal  mandates here in the areas of  transportation telecommunications travel  um  that  that other levels of government  provincial governments i'm positive are  already looking at this about our  federal government also i i think needs  to have a you know a real conversation  about  what the next number of weeks and a  couple of months look like for for  canadians in the areas uh where where  they have leaned in uh with their  federal mandates which have  not had the negative test option um and  and where people have actually uh you  know in some cases lost their their  place of their their employment uh due  to to making uh whatever decision uh  they did so um i i disagree with the  premise of of of the question uh murray  i think as we move forward um this isn't  about whether or not you did the right  thing this is about all of us in society  moving forward together um as i said  many that are vaccinated don't agree  with the the the policies that are in  place um and i've talked to to many of  those individuals as it is so as we uh  you know look ahead in this province we  have  you know everything to attain and to  aspire to and we have all of that  opportunity before us uh  the only thing that would prevent us  from achieving all that we can be is for  us to be  arguing amongst ourselves